traceability.evidence:
1) Story and requirements
- The story file docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md exists and defines acceptance criteria plus requirements:
  - REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE
  - REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION
  - REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION
  - REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
  - REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES
  - REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE

2) Core implementation in valid-annotation-format rule
- File: src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts
- processCommentLine implements JSDoc coexistence logic:
  - Uses normalizeCommentLine per raw line, preserving line-by-line processing:
    ```ts
    rawLines.forEach((rawLine: string) => {
      const normalized = normalizeCommentLine(rawLine);
      pending = processCommentLine({ normalized, pending, context, comment, options });
    });
    ```
  - Detects traceability tags:
    ```ts
    const isStory = /@story\b/.test(normalized);
    const isReq = /@req\b/.test(normalized);
    const isImplements = /@supports\b/.test(normalized);
    ```
  - Handles @supports as single-line, not multi-line (unchanged from earlier stories, preserving backward compatibility).
  - For @story/@req lines, it finalizes any pending annotation, then starts a new PendingAnnotation with value taken only from that line:
    ```ts
    if (isStory || isReq) {
      finalizePendingAnnotation(..., pending);
      const value = normalized.replace(/^@story\b|^@req\b/, "").trim();
      return { type: isStory ? "story" : "req", value, hasValue: value.trim().length > 0 };
    }
    ```
  - JSDoc tag coexistence behavior (directly annotated with this story):
    ```ts
    // Implement JSDoc tag coexistence behavior: terminate @story/@req values when a new non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g., @param, @returns) is encountered.
    // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
    if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
      finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
      return null;
    }
    ```
    This satisfies:
    - REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION (terminates at JSDoc boundary)
    - REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC (non-traceability JSDoc lines are not treated as continuations)
  - Continuation logic applies only when there is a pending annotation and the line is not a JSDoc tag:
    ```ts
    if (pending) {
      const continuation = normalized.trim();
      if (!continuation) {
        return pending;
      }
      const updatedValue = pending.value
        ? `${pending.value} ${continuation}`
        : continuation;
      return { ...pending, value: updatedValue, hasValue: pending.hasValue || continuation.length > 0 };
    }
    ```
    This preserves multi-line values while respecting boundaries, matching REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE and the “Continuation Lines” AC.

3) Boundary-detection helper and line normalization
- File: src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts
- normalizeCommentLine:
  - Trims whitespace, strips inline backtick code spans, and strips a leading '*' for JSDoc, but does not join multiple lines together:
    ```ts
    const trimmed = rawLine.trim();
    if (!trimmed) return "";
    const filtered = trimmed.replace(/`[^`]*`/g, (match) => " ".repeat(match.length));
    const annotationMatch = filtered.match(/@story\b|@req\b|@supports\b/);
    if (!annotationMatch || annotationMatch.index === undefined) {
      const withoutLeadingStar = filtered.replace(/^\*\s?/, "");
      return withoutLeadingStar;
    }
    return filtered.slice(annotationMatch.index);
    ```
  - This preserves per-line boundaries while still locating traceability tags, preventing the old behavior where newlines were stripped and tags concatenated, satisfying REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION at the technical level.

- isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine implements JSDoc boundary detection:
  ```ts
  export function isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): boolean {
    const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
    if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
      return false;
    }
    if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }
  ```
  - Any line that starts with '@' but not @story/@req/@supports is treated as a JSDoc boundary.
  - This directly fulfills REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION and supports REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE.

4) Tests explicitly for Story 022.0 (JSDoc coexistence)
- File: tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts
- Header JSDoc ties tests to this story and its requirements:
  ```js
  * Tests for: docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
  * @story docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
  * @req REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE
  * @req REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION
  * @req REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION
  * @req REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
  * @req REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES
  * @req REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE
  ```

- Valid tests mapping directly to acceptance criteria:
  - **Before Other Tags (AC: Before Other Tags)**
    ```js
    {
      name: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability before other JSDoc tags",
      code: `/**
 * @story docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
 * @req REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE
 * @param {string} id - Identifier for the lookup.
 * @returns {Promise} - Completes when finished.
 */
function fetchById(id) {
  return Promise.resolve();
}`,
    },
    ```
    Confirms annotations work when placed before @param/@returns.

  - **After Other Tags (AC: After Other Tags)**
    ```js
    {
      name: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability after other JSDoc tags",
      code: `/**
 * Fetch a user by id.
 *
 * @param {string} id - Identifier for the lookup.
 * @returns {Promise} - Completes when finished.
 * @story docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
 * @req REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION
 */
function fetchUser(id) {
  return Promise.resolve();
}`,
    },
    ```

  - **Mixed Positions (AC: Mixed Positions)**
    ```js
    {
      name: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] mixed positions of traceability and other JSDoc tags",
      code: `/**
 * Update a record with new data.
 *
 * @story docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
 * @param {string} id - Identifier.
 * @req REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION
 * @param {object} payload - Updated fields.
 * @returns {boolean} - True if updated.
 * @req REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
 */
