- All older tests (for stories 005.0, 010.1, 010.2, etc.) still pass, demonstrating that changes for JSDoc coexistence did not break existing valid annotations, satisfying the “Backward Compatible” acceptance criterion.

7) Bug scenario from Issue #3
- The story’s problem context cites this failure:
  ```js
  /**
   * @req REQ-OPTIMIZATION
   * @param {object} data
   */
  ```
  leading to `Invalid requirement ID "REQ-OPTIMIZATION@param{object}data"`.
- Current behavior:
  - normalizeCommentLine returns "@req REQ-OPTIMIZATION" for the first line, then a non-traceability line beginning with "@param" for the second.
  - processCommentLine first creates a pending @req annotation with value "REQ-OPTIMIZATION".
  - On the `@param` line, isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine returns true, which triggers finalizePendingAnnotation and clears pending; the `@param` text is not appended to the requirement ID.
  - The dedicated test `[REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES] JSDoc tags do not pollute requirement ID when following @req` passes, confirming the bug is resolved and only real format issues still trigger errors.

Altogether, the implementation and tests demonstrate that all acceptance criteria and requirements of Story 022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE are met.
